      ":question/id": "e1df269c-a956-5bf4-be11-d5b8cd2c00b3",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/easy",
      ":question/problem": "Differentiate $- 3 x^{2}\\sin{\\left(x \\right)}$.",
      ":question/worked-solution": "Here, we have the product of the two functions $u(x)=- 3 x^{2}$ and $v(x)=\\sin{\\left(x \\right)}.$ So, we apply the product rule:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}((- 3 x^{2})(\\sin{\\left(x \\right)}))^{'} & =u'(x)\\cdot v(x)+u(x)\\cdot v'(x) \\\\ & =(- 3 x^{2})'\\cdot (\\sin{\\left(x \\right)})+(- 3 x^{2})\\cdot (\\sin{\\left(x \\right)})' \\\\ & =(- 6 x)(\\sin{\\left(x \\right)})+(- 3 x^{2})(\\cos{\\left(x \\right)}) \\\\ & =- 3 x^{2} \\cos{\\left(x \\right)} - 6 x \\sin{\\left(x \\right)}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
